@umamusume_aftermath
title: The final straight
face-image: img/poland/events/umamusume-rice-shower.webp
new-page: true

= One clean run

[? if umamusume_release_response = "Organiser school": By morning, every
district has a training plan, a rest cycle and a closing-straight target. The
organisers embrace the structure. The old guard requests that nobody ever call
candidate selection a *scouting ticket* again.?]

[? if umamusume_release_response = "Consumer-protection bill": The draft does
not ban the game. It requires clear odds, legible prices, spending controls and
a route for parents and players to challenge manipulative design. Fans argue
over the details; lawyers quietly replace every horse pun with statutory
language. It remains a proposal until Parliament acts.?]

[? if umamusume_release_response = "Protected leisure": There is no reaction
clip, no branded stream and no emergency horseshoe logo. The staff go home.
Several return tomorrow with more stamina. Nobody can prove the restraint hurt
the republic.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Return to politics

@third_way_ends
# prose-audit: Grade B — The expiry itself is strong and the successor branches are properly authored. The PSL accounting scene then opens by printing "PSL's leverage is [+ psl_ratchet_score +]/100" — a raw model score shown to the player, which the interaction standard rules out even when, as here, the causes are listed afterwards.
title: Third Way reaches its expiry date
subtitle: Its own cohesion and accumulated disputes decide whether the pact survives
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-kosiniak.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 25
order: 10
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2025 and month >= 6 and coalition_confidence_2025_done = 1 and third_way_split = 0
on-arrival: {!
const thirdWayRoll =
    Math.floor((this.random.uint32() / 4294967296) * 13) - 6;
let splitPressure =
    46 +
    Math.max(0, 55 - (Number(Q.third_way_cohesion) || 0)) -
    Math.max(0, (Number(Q.third_way_cohesion) || 0) - 55) * 0.35 +
    (Number(Q.p2050_coalition_dissent) || 0) * 0.28 +
    (Number(Q.psl_coalition_dissent) || 0) * 0.24 +
    Math.max(0, 35 - (Number(Q.p2050_relation) || 0)) * 0.15 +
    Math.max(0, 35 - (Number(Q.psl_relation) || 0)) * 0.12 +
    Math.max(0, (Number(Q.left_poll) || 0) - 12) * 0.35 +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.party_system_left_pull) || 0) * 0.08 +
    thirdWayRoll;
if (!Q.government_has_confidence) splitPressure += 8;
Q.third_way_split_pressure = Math.round(splitPressure);
Q.third_way_split = splitPressure > 52 ? 1 : 0;
Q.third_way_active = Q.third_way_split ? 0 : 1;
Q.third_way_cohesion += Q.third_way_split ? -25 : 8;
Q.third_way_outgoing_leadership =
    "Szymon Hołownia and Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz as joint electoral principals";
Q.third_way_incoming_leadership = Q.third_way_split
    ? "Hołownia for Poland 2050 and Kosiniak-Kamysz for PSL, negotiating separately"
    : "Hołownia and Kosiniak-Kamysz under a renewed, looser pact";
Q.news_headline = Q.third_way_split
    ? (Q.government_party == "pis"
        ? "PSL and Poland 2050 end Third Way from opposition"
        : (Q.government_has_confidence
            ? "PSL and Poland 2050 end Third Way while both remain in the parliamentary bargain"
            : "PSL and Poland 2050 end Third Way inside a government-formation crisis"))
    : "PSL and Poland 2050 renew Third Way after a close internal reckoning";
!}

= June 2025 — One deadline, two possible futures

The four-election pact has run its course. PSL's county barons and agrarian
conservatives want an independent survival strategy; Poland 2050's founder
loyalists and reform wing want freedom from PSL's social-policy vetoes. Their
poor presidential campaigns mean the joint brand can no longer hide the fact
that the two parties answer to different electorates.

[? if third_way_split: The principals conclude that separate parties now offer
better survival odds. Lewica cannot veto that decision; it can only choose how
to deal with the successor clubs.?]
[? if not third_way_split: The pressure falls just short. Both principals renew
the pact, but only as a looser electoral agreement that preserves more party
autonomy.?]

[? if government_party = "pis": PSL and Poland 2050 are opposition parties.
Their brand decision changes electoral coordination and future majority
building; it does not renegotiate membership in the PiS cabinet.?]
[? if government_party != "pis" and government_has_confidence: The cabinet survived the confidence vote, so
the end of an electoral brand becomes an immediate renegotiation among parties
that still supply its majority.?]
[? if government_party != "pis" and not government_has_confidence: The cabinet has already lost confidence.
Third Way dissolves inside formation talks, where each successor party can
sell its seats separately.?]

[? if government_party = "pis": For Lewica, opposition coordination now
requires separate agreements with PSL and Poland 2050. Playing them against
each other may help one vote and destroy the next common majority.?][? if
government_party != "pis": For Lewica, coalition management now requires
separate majorities with PSL and Poland 2050. Playing them against each other
may win one bill and destroy the government's remaining trust.?]

- @td_bilateral
- @td_psl
- @td_rebuild
- @td_renew
- @td_loose_pact

@td_bilateral
title: Replace the bloc with separate written agreements
subtitle: Treat both successors as equals and make every future majority explicit.
view-if: third_way_split = 1
on-arrival: third_way_response = "Equal bilateral agreements"; psl_relation += 3; p2050_relation += 3; government_coalition_dissent += 2 if government_party != "pis"; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "The Left opens separate channels to PSL and Poland 2050"

We give each successor its own written channel and refuse to crown a preferred
heir. Both can bargain with us; if they share a cabinet, every separate promise
also exposes how little trust remains between them.

- @td_psl_accounting: Open PSL's accumulated account

@td_psl
title: Treat PSL as the only reliable parliamentary hinge
subtitle: Buy a dependable rural hinge by choosing PSL over its former partner.
view-if: third_way_split = 1
on-arrival: third_way_response = "PSL recognised as the parliamentary hinge"; psl_relation += 8; p2050_relation -= 6; rural_support += 2; progressives_dissent += 3; news_headline = "PSL gains another lever over the next parliamentary majority"

We recognise PSL as the partner that can still deliver county networks and
parliamentary votes. Rural channels open; Poland 2050 and our progressives see
us reward the party that carried the social-policy veto.

- @td_psl_accounting: Open PSL's accumulated account

@td_rebuild
title: Encourage a new centrist common list before 2027
subtitle: Help the successors rebuild an electoral shelter voters have just rejected.
view-if: third_way_split = 1
on-arrival: third_way_response = "Attempt to rebuild a centrist electoral shelter"; p2050_relation += 5; psl_relation += 2; ko_relation -= 2; public_trust -= 1; third_way_cohesion += 5; news_headline = "The democratic parties discuss reviving a brand voters have just rejected"

Poland 2050 welcomes our attempt to preserve a centrist lane and PSL keeps the
door ajar. KO resents a rival shelter; voters hear the parties revive a brand
they have only just dissolved.

- @td_psl_accounting: Open PSL's accumulated account

@td_renew
title: Respect the renewed joint list and demand a written social protocol
subtitle: Negotiate with the renewed pact as one partner and prohibit private vetoes.
view-if: third_way_split = 0
on-arrival: third_way_response = "Renewed joint list with a written social protocol"; third_way_cohesion += 4; psl_relation += 2; p2050_relation += 2; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "Lewica treats the renewed alliance as one negotiating partner"
go-to: poland_event_queue

We accept the renewed label and insist that PSL and Poland 2050 sign the same
social terms. Their pact gains a reason to exist; neither party can sell us a
private veto after the agreement is public.

@td_loose_pact
title: Work with each party separately while tolerating the common brand
subtitle: Keep two parliamentary channels open and let the electoral label weaken.
view-if: third_way_split = 0
on-arrival: third_way_response = "Separate channels under a loose electoral pact"; p2050_relation += 3; psl_relation += 1; third_way_cohesion -= 2; government_coalition_dissent += 1 if government_party != "pis"; news_headline = "The renewed Third Way survives through separate parliamentary channels"
go-to: poland_event_queue

We tolerate the common logo and negotiate underneath it with two parties.
Poland 2050 gains room from PSL; the pact survives on paper while each bill
teaches its members to act separately.

@td_psl_accounting
title: PSL presents the accumulated account
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
let ratchet =
    (Number(Q.psl_coalition_dissent) || 0) * 0.45 +
    (Q.government_party == "pis"
        ? 0
        : (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) * 0.24) +
    Math.max(0, 45 - (Number(Q.psl_relation) || 0)) * 0.35 +
    Math.max(0, 35 - (Number(Q.rural_support) || 0)) * 0.18;
if (Q.government_party != "pis" && Q.coalition_break_threat) ratchet += 10;
if (Q.government_party != "pis" && Q.abortion_cabinet_deadline) ratchet += 7;
if (Q.third_way_response == "PSL recognised as the parliamentary hinge") {
    ratchet += 8;
}
if (Q.third_way_response == "Equal bilateral agreements") {
    ratchet -= 4;
}
Q.psl_ratchet_score = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(100, Math.round(ratchet))
);
Q.news_headline =
    "PSL converts the end of Third Way into a list of parliamentary terms";
!}

= The price was accumulated, not invented today

PSL's leverage is **[+ psl_ratchet_score +]/100**. It comes from farm protests,
the abortion roll call, the presidential result and its relationship with
Lewica[? if government_party != "pis": , as well as the cabinet's own dissent?].
The Left's opening line—**[+
third_way_response +]**—changes the negotiation, but does not erase that
history.

[? if government_party != "pis" and coalition_break_threat: PSL's negotiators quote the earlier threat to
leave government as proof that every progressive vote now carries a cabinet
price.?]
[? if government_party != "pis" and abortion_cabinet_deadline: The spring abortion deadline remains live.
PSL will not sign language that turns its free vote into automatic expulsion.?]
[? if psl_relation >= 55: The bilateral relationship is good enough for a
written trade; PSL does not need to manufacture a public humiliation.?]
[? if psl_relation < 35: Private channels are weak. Every demand is therefore
also a press conference and an invitation for the right to bid.?]

- @td_protocol
- @td_hold_line
- @td_roll_calls

@td_protocol
title: Sign a rural-social protocol without granting another rights veto
subtitle: Cost: 1 budget capacity in government, otherwise 1 resource.
choose-if: (left_in_government = 1 and budget >= 1) or (left_in_government = 0 and resources >= 1)
unavailable-subtitle: No material offer can be attached to the protocol.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.left_in_government) Q.budget -= 1;
else Q.resources -= 1;
Q.psl_protocol_2025 =
    "Rural services and farm bargaining; no new social-policy veto";
Q.psl_relation += 6;
Q.psl_coalition_dissent -= 5;
if (Q.government_party != "pis") Q.government_coalition_dissent -= 3;
Q.rural_support += 3;
Q.progressives_dissent += 2;
Q.psl_ratchet_score = Math.max(0, Q.psl_ratchet_score - 10);
Q.news_headline =
    "A material PSL agreement draws a line around its conservative veto";
!}
go-to: poland_event_queue

We fund rural services and farm bargaining while writing that no new rights
veto follows. PSL takes a material win; our progressives accept the price
because the boundary is finally public.

@td_hold_line
title: Refuse new concessions and test whether PSL will actually leave
subtitle: Party unity rises; partner dissent and early-election risk rise, with cabinet dissent only if governing together.
on-arrival: psl_protocol_2025 = "No renegotiation beyond the 2023 agreement"; party_unity += 4; psl_relation -= 9; psl_coalition_dissent += 8; government_coalition_dissent += 7 if government_party != "pis"; early_election_risk += 7; razem_cooperation += 2; psl_ratchet_score += 8; news_headline = "The Left ends the concession cycle and opens a survival test"
go-to: poland_event_queue

We refuse another payment for votes already promised in 2023. The Left closes
ranks and PSL must either retreat or prove that its threats can end the common
majority.

@td_roll_calls
title: Replace private vetoes with published bill-by-bill agreements
subtitle: More visible instability; less room for surprise partner blackmail.
on-arrival: {!
Q.psl_protocol_2025 = "Published bill-by-bill support ledger";
Q.public_trust += 3;
Q.constitutional_restraint += 2;
Q.psl_relation += 1;
if (Q.government_party != "pis") Q.government_coalition_dissent += 3;
Q.progressives_dissent -= 2;
Q.barons_dissent += 2;
Q.psl_ratchet_score = Math.max(
    0,
    (Number(Q.psl_ratchet_score) || 0) - 4
);
Q.news_headline =
    "Coalition disagreement receives a public voting ledger";
!}
go-to: poland_event_queue

Every bargain becomes a published roll call instead of a private veto. The
cabinet looks less stable, but PSL and Lewica can no longer tell different
stories about the same bill.

@presidential_protests_2025
# prose-audit: Grade C — The distinction between documented commission errors and a delegitimising claim is the whole point of the event and it is made cleanly; the protest lawyers and commission members remain unnamed.
title: Protests, recounts and the size of the claim
subtitle: Real polling-station errors meet a demand to annul the whole result
face-image: img/poland/events/million-hearts-march-2023.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 40
order: 8
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2025 and month >= 6 and pres_2025_runoff_done = 1 and presidential_protests_2025_done = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.presidential_protests_2025_done = 1;
const margin = Math.abs(Number(Q.pres_2025_runoff_margin) || 2);
Q.pres_2025_protest_scale = margin < 2
    ? "close enough that arithmetic alone sustains the doubt"
    : (margin < 5
        ? "narrow enough for the errors to be argued about"
        : "wide enough that no commission error could have changed it");
Q.pres_2025_recount_commissions = 13;
Q.institutional_trust = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) - 3
);
Q.institutional_issue_salience =
    (Number(Q.institutional_issue_salience) || 0) + 5;
Q.news_headline =
    "Thousands of protests reach the Supreme Court over the presidential count";
!}

= June 2025 — Two different claims wearing the same words

The margin was **[+ pres_2025_runoff_margin +] points** — [+
pres_2025_protest_scale +]. Tens of thousands of electoral protests are lodged
with the Supreme Court. Most are form letters. A small number are not:
volunteers comparing published commission protocols against the national
totals find precincts where the two candidates' figures were transposed, where
a total does not reconcile, where a protocol was signed with an obvious
arithmetic error. Recounts are ordered in **[+ pres_2025_recount_commissions
+]** commissions.

Both facts are true at once and they are not the same fact. Some commissions
got it wrong, as they do in every election, and the errors run in both
directions. Separately, a political claim is circulating that the errors are
evidence the national result was manufactured — a claim whose size does not
depend on the evidence and which will not be retired if the recounts confirm
the winner.

[? if referendum_2023_stance = "Organised ballot refusal" or referendum_2023_stance = "Refusal plus counter-questions": We
spent the 2023 campaign teaching our own voters how commission procedure works
and how a refusal is recorded. Several thousand of those people are the
volunteers now photographing protocols.?]
[? if electoral_confidence >= 65: Public confidence in the count is high enough
that a documented error still reads as an error rather than as proof.?]
[? if electoral_confidence < 50: Confidence in the count was already low before
a single protocol was photographed, which is the condition in which arithmetic
stops persuading anybody.?]
[? if left_in_government = 1: Our ministers are in a government that will be
accused of stealing the election if it defends the count, and of abandoning
the state if it does not.?][? if left_in_government = 0: We are outside the
government and outside the Palace, which makes it cheap for us to be correct
and easy for us to be ignored.?]

- @protests_verify
- @protests_amplify
- @protests_dismiss

@protests_verify
title: Fund the protocol verification and publish every error found, in both directions
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Separates documented errors from the delegitimising claim by proving the errors were counted.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: No legal or volunteer capacity is free for a national protocol audit.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; institutional_trust += 7; judicial_legitimacy += 4; constitutional_restraint += 5; public_trust += 4; media_capacity += 2; electoral_confidence += 8; news_headline = "The published error audit runs in both directions and closes the arithmetic"

Our volunteers do the least glamorous work in politics: photograph every
disputed protocol, compare it to the published total, publish the corrections
including the ones that favour the candidate we opposed. The recounts
confirm the pattern — real errors, no direction, no scale.

It does not persuade the people who wanted a stolen election. It gives every
institution, journalist and future court a document that exists, and it means
the party that ran the audit is not the party that has to be believed on
trust.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the protocol audit

@protests_amplify
title: Treat the errors as grounds to question the whole result
subtitle: Available and satisfying if the margin was thin; it puts our name on a claim we cannot subsequently retire.
on-arrival: electoral_confidence -= 14; institutional_trust -= 8; constitutional_restraint -= 8; judicial_legitimacy -= 4; left_poll_momentum += 0.15; public_trust -= 2; far_right_agenda += 3; news_headline = "The Left joins the demand that the presidential result be annulled"

We say the count cannot be trusted. Given the protocols and the margin the
sentence is not absurd, and it is enormously popular with people who cannot
accept the outcome.

The claim is now ours as well. When the Supreme Court confirms the result, we
will either abandon our own supporters or continue disputing a certified
presidential election — and the next time somebody makes this argument against
a result we like, our words will be read back to us.

- @poland_event_queue: Join the annulment demand

@protests_dismiss
title: Refuse the whole subject and treat every protest as bad faith
subtitle: Defends the result at the cost of the volunteers who found genuine errors.
on-arrival: electoral_confidence += 3; institutional_trust += 2; constitutional_restraint += 3; public_trust -= 2; movement_autonomy -= 4; far_right_agenda += 2; anti_system_trust -= 3; news_headline = "The Left dismisses the electoral protests as a manufactured campaign"

The line is short: the result stands, the protests are a campaign, move on. It
is defensible, it protects the winner's legitimacy, and it takes about a day.

It also tells several thousand volunteers who spent a fortnight checking
protocols — many of them ours — that noticing an error is indistinguishable
from denying an election. They stop checking. The next time the errors are not
random, nobody is looking.

- @poland_event_queue: Close the subject
